{% doc %}
  The tickets whose conversation contains this text, as a lookup keyed on
  ticket id.

  Searching bodies cannot be done the way the rest of the search box
  works. A ticket carries a haystack of its own number, subject and
  requester, kept current on every message, but putting message bodies in
  it would grow one column without limit and rewrite it on every reply.
  So bodies are searched where they live and the answer is joined in
  memory.

  Only the ids come back. The caller already holds the tickets, and it
  only has to mark the ones that matched.

  Capped, like every other query here. A search matching more than the
  cap still finds the most recent matches, which is the half an agent
  typing into a search box wants.

  Private notes are searched too. They can only ever mark a ticket the
  viewer was already being shown, because the queue is scoped to their
  departments before this runs.

  @param {string} [query] - Text to look for, already lowercased
  @param {number} [limit] - How many matching messages to consider
{% enddoc %}
{% liquid
  assign hits = {}
  if query == blank
    return hits
  endif

  assign fetch = limit | default: 300
  assign sort = { "created_at": { "order": "DESC" } }
  graphql result = 'modules/support/messages/search', body: query, sort: sort, limit: fetch, page: 1, id: null, ticket_id: null, contact_id: null, created_at_gte: null, kind: null, message_id_header: null, message_id_headers: null

  for message in result.records.results
    assign hits[message.ticket_id] = true
  endfor

  return hits
%}
